{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.p1_nonlinear_uniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.p1_nonlinear_uniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.p1_nonlinear_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.p1_nonlinear_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L68-L82","doc":"**Nonlinear estimate + uniqueness** ([`prop:p1-nonlinear-uniqueness`]).\n\n(a), (b) surface the upstream analytic inputs; (c) uniqueness is\n*derived* from the Gronwall distance bound: `dist(0) = 0` forces\n`dist(t) ≤ 0 · G(t) = 0`, and non-negativity gives equality. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-ns-nonlinear-uniqueness","label":"prop:q-ns-nonlinear-uniqueness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p1-nonlinear-uniqueness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.distance_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.distance_bound","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L65-L65","doc":"**Gronwall distance bound (the genuine input for uniqueness):**\n`dist(t) ≤ dist(0) · G(t)` for `t ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.growth","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Gronwall growth factor for the solution distance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.distance_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.distance_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Distances are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.distance_v1_v2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.distance_v1_v2","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L58-L58","doc":"`L²` distance of two divergence-free solutions with common data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.enstrophy_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.enstrophy_bound","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L56-L56","doc":"**(b) — upstream input (Gronwall on the enstrophy):**\n`Ω(t) ≤ Ω(0) e^{Λ_q t}` for `t ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.Λ_q_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.Λ_q_eq","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.Λ_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.Λ_q","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Exponential growth rate, pinned to the manuscript value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.Ω","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.Ω","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Enstrophy `Ω(t) = ‖d_q v(t)‖²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.q_ladyzhenskaya","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.q_ladyzhenskaya","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L48-L48","doc":"**(a) — upstream input:** `q`-Ladyzhenskaya inequality\n`‖B(v)‖ ≤ C_q ‖v‖ ‖d_q v‖`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.B_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.B_norm","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.dv_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.dv_norm","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.v_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.v_norm","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Velocity / gradient / advection norms as functions of time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.ν_q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.ν_q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.ν_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.ν_q","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Kinematic viscosity `ν_q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.C_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.C_q","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Sobolev constant `C_q = (Σ_k [k]_q^{−2})^{1/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.E_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.E_0","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Initial energy `E₀ = ‖v₀‖²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P1NonlinearUniquenessContext","kind":"class","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p1_nonlinear_uniqueness.lean#L29-L66","doc":"Hypotheses for the nonlinear estimate + uniqueness lemma (post-wall\n`ℝ` block — `Real.exp`/order are genuinely archimedean, §7c).  The\nLadyzhenskaya and enstrophy estimates are upstream analytic inputs;\nthe Gronwall distance bound is the genuine input from which\nuniqueness is *derived*. ","signatureChunk":0}]}